WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.268
Local quantized model names often include labels such as Q2, Q3, Q4, Q5, Q6,

00:00:05.268 --> 00:00:06.007
or Q8.

00:00:06.007 --> 00:00:10.436
At a high level, the number indicates the approximate weight precision family:

00:00:10.436 --> 00:00:14.128
lower levels use less memory and usually accept more approximation,

00:00:14.128 --> 00:00:17.820
while higher levels retain more information and require more space.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.034
Suffixes identify specific methods, group sizes,

00:00:20.034 --> 00:00:25.572
or mixed-precision choices and are meaningful only in the context of that format and runtime.

00:00:25.572 --> 00:00:30.002
Q4 variants are often a practical starting point because they provide substantial

00:00:30.002 --> 00:00:34.062
memory savings while preserving useful quality for many models and tasks.

00:00:34.062 --> 00:00:36.647
That is a heuristic, not a guarantee.

00:00:36.647 --> 00:00:41.446
A particular architecture may respond differently, two Q4 methods may not behave identically,

00:00:41.446 --> 00:00:46.614
and a coding or reasoning task may reveal losses that casual conversation does not.

00:00:46.614 --> 00:00:49.936
Q2 and Q3 can make otherwise inaccessible models fit,

00:00:49.936 --> 00:00:52.151
but aggressive compression increases quality risk.

00:00:52.151 --> 00:00:56.581
Q5 and Q6 consume more memory and may preserve behavior more closely.

00:00:56.581 --> 00:01:01.011
Q8 often approaches the memory cost of higher precision while remaining useful

00:01:01.011 --> 00:01:03.964
when quality is prioritized and hardware has room.

00:01:03.964 --> 00:01:08.763
Speed does not increase monotonically as bits decrease; kernel efficiency, offload, memory fit,

00:01:08.763 --> 00:01:10.609
and hardware support all matter.

00:01:10.609 --> 00:01:12.824
Choose candidates around the hardware boundary.

00:01:12.824 --> 00:01:15.039
If Q5 fits with context headroom,

00:01:15.039 --> 00:01:19.100
compare it with Q4 rather than assuming the smaller one wins.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:22.053
If only Q3 fits fully on the GPU,

00:01:22.053 --> 00:01:26.852
compare its quality and speed with a smaller model at Q4 or Q5.

00:01:26.852 --> 00:01:31.282
Quantization level is one decision among model family, parameter count, context, runtime,

00:01:31.282 --> 00:01:32.020
and workload.
